hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"146","Kāna Rasūlullāh ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-salam yaʿūdh al-Ḥasan wa-l-Ḥusayn: \Aʿūdhukumā bikalimātillāhi al-tāmmah"," min kulli shayṭān wa hāmmah"," wa min kulli ʿayn lāmmah.\"". The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to seek refuge for al-Hasan and al-Husayn"," saying: \""I seek protection for you both by the perfect words of Allah"," from every devil and poisonous creature"," and from every envious eye.\"""""
"147","Lā ba'sa ṭahūrun in shā Allāh. Do not worry, it will be a purification (for you), Allah willing. Reference: Al-Bukhari, cf. Al-Asqalani Fathul-Bari 10/118."
